00:23:50.650 --> 00:23:53.530
all lack a bit of a certain Crawford-ness.
都缺少了一点某种克劳福德式的特质。

513
00:23:54.270 --> 00:23:54.590
Yeah.
是的。

514
00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:56.370
But there's more bad news.
但还有更多坏消息。

515
00:23:56.950 --> 00:24:00.010
Everyone finds out that they have to come in on Saturday.
每个人都发现他们周六得来加班。

516
00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:02.710
And this is not a joke this time.
而且这次不是开玩笑。

517
00:24:02.710 --> 00:24:05.730
This is not Michael setting the stage for a dinner party trap.
这不是迈克尔在为晚宴陷阱做铺垫。

518
00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:06.850
This is real.
这是真的。

519
00:24:07.010 --> 00:24:08.350
We have to work on Saturday.
我们周六得工作。

520
00:24:08.910 --> 00:24:10.070
Yeah, Oscar is livid.
是的，奥斯卡气炸了。

521
00:24:10.250 --> 00:24:11.710
Angela says it's ridiculous.
安吉拉说这太荒谬了。

522
00:24:12.130 --> 00:24:16.830
There's a lot of hubbub in the bullpen because they find out on Saturday they're going to
办公大区里一片喧嚣，因为他们发现周六他们必须把所有的辛勤工作、所有的销售业绩

523
00:24:16.830 --> 00:24:20.810
have to take all of their hard work, all of the sales they made, and they're going to
都把功劳记在网站头上。

524
00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:22.450
have to give the credit to the website.
他们得把这一切都录入进去，就好像是网站做的一样。

525
00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:25.450
They're going to log it all in as if the website did it.
是的，珍娜，会计部有一个场景。

526
00:24:25.850 --> 00:24:27.890
Yeah, Jenna, there's a scene in accounting.
你知道的，奥斯卡说他气炸了。

527
00:24:28.110 --> 00:24:29.650
You know, Oscar's saying he's livid.
安吉拉说这太荒谬了。

528
00:24:29.810 --> 00:24:30.970
Angela says this is ridiculous.
有一系列被删减的片段。

529
00:24:30.970 --> 00:24:33.390
There is a series of deleted scenes.
珍娜，这是帕姆和安吉拉之间的一条贯穿剧情。

530
00:24:33.790 --> 00:24:36.390
Jenna, it's a runner between Pam and Angela.
是什么？

531
00:24:36.750 --> 00:24:37.710
What is it?
嗯，显然，不管出于什么原因，今天是安吉拉就是讨厌

532
00:24:38.150 --> 00:24:43.470
Well, apparently, for whatever reason, this is one of those days where Angela just hates
帕姆的日子。

533
00:24:43.470 --> 00:24:43.910
Pam.
就像，仅仅听到你的声音一样。

534
00:24:45.550 --> 00:24:47.810
Like, just the sound of your voice.
好吧，安吉拉和奥斯卡在说话，帕姆把头探过隔板。

535
00:24:47.950 --> 00:24:52.090
Okay, so Angela and Oscar are talking, and Pam pokes her head over the partition.
对吧？

536
00:24:52.530 --> 00:24:53.030
Right?
她想加入对话。

537
00:24:53.290 --> 00:24:55.230
She wants to get in on the convo.
这就是安吉拉说的话。

538
00:24:55.490 --> 00:24:57.190
And this is what Angela says.
山姆，你能放一下片段吗？

539
00:24:57.430 --> 00:24:58.610
Sam, can you play the clip?
所以，这是肯定的了？

540
00:24:59.530 --> 00:25:00.530
So, it's definite?
看起来是这样。

541
00:25:00.950 --> 00:25:01.790
Looks like it.
糟了。

542
00:25:02.170 --> 00:25:02.470
Shoot.
我和吉姆本打算这周末去樱花节的。

543
00:25:02.990 --> 00:25:05.570
Jim and I were going to go to the Cherry Blossom Festival this weekend.
我很遗憾。

544
00:25:05.850 --> 00:25:06.430
I'm sorry.
你的声音？

545
00:25:06.670 --> 00:25:07.650
Your voice?
就像那样在我头顶上方？

546
00:25:07.850 --> 00:25:09.190
Over my head like that?
抱歉。

547
00:25:11.320 --> 00:25:11.800
Sorry.
这难道不搞笑吗？

548
00:25:15.720 --> 00:25:16.720
Isn't that hilarious?
就像，你在我身后说话的声音让我无法忍受。

549
00:25:16.800 --> 00:25:20.120
Like, just your voice behind me was more than I could take.
呃。

550
00:25:20.360 --> 00:25:20.740
Ugh.
哼。

551
00:25:20.960 --> 00:25:23.200
Now that I hear that, I remember shooting that.
听到这个，我想起当时拍这幕的情景了。

552
00:25:24.880 --> 00:25:26.360
There's going to be another one.
还有一个。

553
00:25:26.360 --> 00:25:27.520
I'm going to save it for later.
我要把它留到后面用。

554
00:25:28.460 --> 00:25:33.380
So, Ryan has delivered this news, and he's being super upbeat about it, but Jim's going
所以，瑞安传达了这消息，而且他对此态度超级乐观，但吉姆打算

555
00:25:33.380 --> 00:25:34.600
to confront him in the kitchen.
在厨房找他质问。

556
00:25:35.080 --> 00:25:35.300
Yeah.
对。

557
00:25:35.660 --> 00:25:39.160
Jim's like, hey, man, you mind if I run something by you?
吉姆就像是，嘿，老兄，介意我跟你商量个事吗？

558
00:25:39.500 --> 00:25:43.560
Ryan, of course, is in his, like, super, he's just a lot in this episode.
瑞安当然处于那种，超级，他在这一集里实在太过了。

559
00:25:43.580 --> 00:25:44.380
He's like, love it.
他就像是，太棒了。

560
00:25:44.520 --> 00:25:44.900
Go.
说吧。

561
00:25:45.200 --> 00:25:45.520
Right?
对吧？

562
00:25:45.960 --> 00:25:49.860
And Jim's like, I kind of feel like what we have going for us is our customer service,
然后吉姆就说，我总觉得我们的优势在于客户服务，

563
00:25:49.860 --> 00:25:53.920
and no matter how we change this up, I don't know that a website's going to be able to
不管我们怎么改变，我不知道网站是否能够

564
00:25:53.920 --> 00:25:54.600
replace that.
取代这一点。

565
00:25:55.080 --> 00:25:57.600
Ryan goes, I can tell you thought a lot about this.
瑞安就说，我看得出来你对此深思熟虑过。

566
00:25:57.780 --> 00:25:58.560
I appreciate that.
我很感激。

567
00:25:58.820 --> 00:25:59.100
Thanks.
谢谢。

568
00:25:59.600 --> 00:26:01.320
David Wallace does, too.
大卫·华莱士也是这么想的。

569
00:26:01.660 --> 00:26:03.240
You told him at the Christmas party, right?
你是在圣诞派对上告诉他的，对吧？

570
00:26:03.880 --> 00:26:04.720
Jim's like, uh.
吉姆就，呃。

571
00:26:05.160 --> 00:26:06.820
And Ryan's like, yeah, watch your back, Jim.
然后瑞安就说，嘿，小心点，吉姆。

572
00:26:07.220 --> 00:26:08.060
I'm just kidding.
我开玩笑呢。

573
00:26:08.480 --> 00:26:08.920
Yeah.
是啊。

574
00:26:09.400 --> 00:26:12.500
I mean, Ryan has it out for Jim.
我的意思是，瑞安跟吉姆杠上了。

575
00:26:12.740 --> 00:26:14.120
You know, here's a bit of trivia.
你知道，这里有个小花絮。

576
00:26:14.480 --> 00:26:19.440
We would have had a Christmas episode, but we didn't because of the writer's strike.
我们本来应该有一集圣诞特辑的，但因为编剧罢工没拍成。

577
00:26:19.800 --> 00:26:20.220
I know.
我知道。

578
00:26:20.340 --> 00:26:21.280
I'm so bummed about that.
我对此超级沮丧。

579
00:26:21.420 --> 00:26:21.600
Yeah.
是啊。

580
00:26:21.760 --> 00:26:24.440
So that's why this season does not have a Christmas episode.
所以这就是为什么这一季没有圣诞特辑。

581
00:26:24.780 --> 00:26:25.260
Yeah.
对。

582
00:26:25.960 --> 00:26:32.340
Well, now we move into the conference room, and Michael, this really made me laugh.
好吧，现在我们来到会议室，迈克尔这段真的把我逗笑了。

583
00:26:32.580 --> 00:26:36.720
He's sort of trying to sympathize with Ryan, why people are feeling resentful towards Ryan.
他有点试图去同情瑞安，理解为什么大家对瑞安感到不满。

584
00:26:36.940 --> 00:26:39.220
And then he makes this speech.
然后他发表了这段演讲。

585
00:26:39.660 --> 00:26:45.380
And Jenna, I could not imagine being introduced by my boss for a meeting like this.
珍娜，我简直无法想象我的老板会这样介绍我开会。

586
00:26:45.680 --> 00:26:47.880
Ladies and gentlemen, may I have your attention, please?
女士们先生们，请大家注意好吗？

587
00:26:47.880 --> 00:26:52.600
I know that a lot of you are very angry with Ryan because he is the reason we all have to come in tomorrow.
我知道你们很多人对瑞安非常生气，因为他是我们明天都得来上班的原因。

588
00:26:52.800 --> 00:27:01.040
However, I swear to God, if any of you hurts him in any way emotionally or taunts him or makes fun of his height or his half beard or...
然而，我向上帝发誓，如果你们当中有人在情感上伤害他，或者嘲弄他，或者取笑他的身高、他的半边胡子，或者...

589
00:27:01.040 --> 00:27:02.960
I love his half beard.
我喜欢他的半边胡子。

590
00:27:03.180 --> 00:27:03.620
I know.
我知道。

591
00:27:03.760 --> 00:27:05.380
If you make fun of his half beard.
如果你取笑他的半边胡子。

592
00:27:06.020 --> 00:27:08.020
I saw Oscar start to break.
我看到奥斯卡开始笑场了。

593
00:27:08.580 --> 00:27:09.400
That's huge.
这太难得了。

594
00:27:09.580 --> 00:27:09.980
Yes.
是的。

595
00:27:10.140 --> 00:27:15.520
But I know Oscar's tells so well because we sat next to each other for the whole run of the show.
但我太了解奥斯卡的破功小动作了，因为整部剧拍摄期间我们都坐在一起。

596
00:27:15.520 --> 00:27:20.380
So one of the things he does when something makes him laugh, but he's trying not to laugh,
所以当有什么事让他想笑但他又在极力忍住时，

597
00:27:20.520 --> 00:27:23.880
is he does this little thing with his head where he kind of nods his head down.
他会做这样一个头部的小动作，把头往下微点。

598
00:27:24.600 --> 00:27:26.680
And it's so slight, you guys.
而且极其微小，伙计们。

599
00:27:26.860 --> 00:27:27.720
It's so slight.
真的极其微小。

600
00:27:27.940 --> 00:27:31.780
But when Michael says the part about the beard, Oscar does that little head nod thing.
但当迈克尔说到胡子那部分时，奥斯卡就做了那个点头的小动作。

601
00:27:31.900 --> 00:27:34.380
And I was like, oh, Oscar, I see you.
当时我就想，哦，奥斯卡，我看到你了。

602
00:27:34.900 --> 00:27:41.480
After his lovely introduction, Ryan starts defending Dunder Mifflin 2.0 very passionately.
在她可爱的介绍之后，瑞恩开始非常激情地为“邓德米福林 2.0”辩护。

603
00:27:42.140 --> 00:27:42.300
Yeah.
是啊。

604
00:27:42.480 --> 00:27:43.780
And he's going on and on.
而且他说个没完。

605
00:27:44.020 --> 00:27:45.800
He knows the website was hacked.
他知道网站被黑了。

606
00:27:45.980 --> 00:27:47.260
He's trying to defend it.
他还在极力辩解。

607
00:27:47.840 --> 00:27:50.620
Jenna, I have a conference table catch during his speech.
珍娜，在他演讲的时候，会议桌有个穿帮镜头。

608
00:27:50.840 --> 00:27:51.340
What?
什么？

609
00:27:51.860 --> 00:27:53.340
Four minutes, 30 seconds.
四分三十秒。

610
00:27:53.720 --> 00:27:56.620
There are two coffee mugs on the conference table.
会议桌上有两个咖啡杯。

611
00:27:57.120 --> 00:27:59.120
Any guesses whose they are?
猜猜是谁的？

612
00:27:59.360 --> 00:28:02.260
Well, one of them is Pam's pink mug because I saw it.
嗯，其中一个是帕姆的粉色杯子，因为我看到了。

613
00:28:02.260 --> 00:28:08.280
I did not notice another one because I only look at myself when I'm watching the group scenes.
我没注意到另一个，因为我看群戏时只看自己。

614
00:28:08.440 --> 00:28:10.020
But I did see that I had my mug.
但我确实看到我拿了自己的杯子。

615
00:28:10.280 --> 00:28:11.180
So does Jim.
吉姆也是。

616
00:28:11.500 --> 00:28:14.520
Oh, no one else has a coffee mug.
哦，其他人都没有咖啡杯。

617
00:28:14.760 --> 00:28:15.800
Just Jim and Pam.
只有吉姆和帕姆。

618
00:28:16.340 --> 00:28:22.360
And I started thinking, when did you ever see anyone with a beverage in the conference room except a party?
然后我开始琢磨，除了开派对，你什么时候在会议室里看到过任何人拿着饮料？

619
00:28:22.600 --> 00:28:23.500
All the time.
一直都有啊。

620
00:28:23.700 --> 00:28:28.920
I always brought my mug into the conference room, Angela, because I could actually drink coffee during the scene.
